==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} To [[accelerate]] or [[speed]] up quickly or [[suddenly]].
#: {{ux|en|You're going to have to '''gun it''' to pick up that much speed in such a short distance.}}

{{cln|en|predicates}}

Back in 1976 Racing a 1971 Mach one Mustang in London Keith Mace & Paul Kennet had just seen a movie regarding speed of bullets and during the race Keith who was the driver and was winning shouted out gunit. Later during a race car meeting announced the word gunit which then became the in word for accelerated speed. This has now become the standard for acceleration.